xactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-scalar-localization"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-scalar-localization"],"id":"long.lem-scalar-localization","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 10.13 (Denominator complement survives scaling)","locator":"Long record Lemma 10.13, p. 119, label lem:scalar-localization","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For $x:\\mathbb Q$, $c:\\mathbb Z$, $H:\\mathbb N$: if $H\\mid x.\\mathrm{den}$ and $(c\\cdot x).\\mathrm{den}\\mid H$ ; i.e. multiplying by the integer $c$ shrinks the displayed denominator down *into* $H$ ; then the **complementary** denominator factor $x.\\mathrm{den}/H$ divides $c$:\n$$\nH\\mid x.\\mathrm{den} \\ \\land\\ (c\\cdot x).\\mathrm{den}\\mid H \\implies x.\\mathrm{den}/H \\mid |c|.\n$$\nEquivalently, writing $D=x.\\mathrm{den}/H$, we have $D\\mid c$, so $t=c/D$ is an integer and $Hcx=t\\,x.\\mathrm{num}$. Here $H>0$ follows from $H\\mid x.\\mathrm{den}$, since the reduced denominator is positive.*\n\n***Scope.** This is elementary rational arithmetic, independent of the problem. If $c\\ne0$, divisibility gives the size bound $|c|\\ge x.\\mathrm{den}/H$. The nonzero condition is essential: $c=0$ clears every denominator and satisfies the divisibility conclusion without any positive lower bound on $|c|$. The lemma therefore constrains denominator clearing by a nonzero bounded multiplier, not arbitrary multiplication. **Object or representation:** about a *representation* ; pure denominator bookkeeping for $\\mathbb Q$, with zero problem-specific content; the upstream primitive is the domain-neutral extraction this lemma builds on.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-scalar-localization","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-scalar-localization","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-scalar-localization%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_scalar_localization%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-scalar-localization%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_scalar_localization%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_scalar_localization"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-scalar-localization","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-scalar-localization%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_scalar_localization_size_bound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-scalar-localization%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_scalar_localization_size_bound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_scalar_localization_size_bound"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-scalar-localization","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-scalar-localization%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_scalar_localization_zero_degenerate%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:571